  "curriculum": "The regular Dutch part-time BSc totals 180 EC. Twenty-two compulsory 5 EC subject courses give 110 EC; Basic Academic Skills (5 EC), Methods and Techniques of Research (15 EC) and its sequel (5 EC) give 25 EC; the six free slots total 30 EC; the thesis is 15 EC. Seven thematic learning lines organize the same degree, with no separate routes. The annual schedule’s table and official course listings identify MB2512 and MB2212 despite stale footnote codes MB2502 and MB2202.",
  "progression": "In the illustrative six-year sequence, MB0622 is taken in year one. The year-three MB0226 needs at least 30 EC including MB0622. Year-five MB2212 follows MB0226, and the year-six 15 EC thesis needs at least 150 EC including MB0226. The 60 EC foundation certificate requires Management and Organization, Entrepreneurship and 50 additional eligible subject or skills credits, excluding free electives. Mandatory in-person meetings in MB0226 are course obligations within its credits.",
